## Fraud Detection Model Monitoring Stack
This project implements a complete Prometheus and Grafana monitoring stack for a fraud-detection model. It uses a custom Flask metric emitter to generate live machine learning signals and exposes them to Prometheus for scraping and Grafana for visualization.

Architecture & Components
metric-emitter: A Python/Flask application that exposes real-time ML metrics (flask_http_request_total, prediction_accuracy, data_drift_score, and model_inference_duration_seconds). A background thread updates these values every 5 seconds.

mon-prometheus: A Prometheus instance configured to scrape the metric-emitter service every 5 seconds over the internal Docker network (http://prometheus:9090).

mon-grafana: A Grafana instance configured via its API to connect to Prometheus and display live dashboard panels.

